    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born of the 1830 revolution against the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>, it was recognised as neutral by the great powers in 1839.</li><li>It was continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>’s first industrial nation and, through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii">Leopold II</a>, the ruler of the Congo, where forced labour cost countless lives.</li><li>Conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and French speakers turned it into a federal state in 1993, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> became home to the EU and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>’s line from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> to Mechelen, opened in May 1835, was the first steam passenger railway in continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, built and run by the state itself.</p></aside>
    </section>

